"""Render the property-focused OpenAlex search report from frozen receipts."""
import json


def render_property_survey(root, datasets, date, cell):
    manifest = json.loads((root / 'research/openalex_property_20261101/search_manifest.json').read_text())
    by_id = {d['id']: d for d in datasets}
    chosen = [by_id[i] for i in manifest['new_dataset_ids']]
    def ref(ident):
        d = by_id[ident]
        return f'[{d["name"]}](catalog/{d["category"]}.md#{ident})'
    lines = ['# Specialized materials property datasets: an OpenAlex search', '', f'Checked {date}. **{len(chosen)} new dataset/release records**, plus an expanded DDSE/DigBat lineage record. The catalog now contains {len(datasets)} records. This is a local research expansion, not an exhaustive census of published data.', '',
             '[Search the additions](https://usccolumbia.github.io/matverse/?q=property-focused) · [Search receipt](../research/openalex_property_20261101/search_manifest.json) · [Retrieved-work ledger](../research/openalex_property_20261101/retrieved_works.json) · [Selected-paper OpenAlex checks](../research/openalex_property_20261101/selected_paper_openalex_checks.json)', '',
             '## Abstract', '',
             'Starting from the DDSE paper, this search examines specialized property datasets across electrochemical transport, ferroic and optical response, thermal and magnetic properties, alloy mechanics, hydrogen storage and combustion. The useful distinction is between measured properties with experimental conditions, calculated responses attached to structures, and literature records attached mainly to compositions. These populations support different tasks. Their headline counts cannot be combined into a number of independent crystals.', '',
             '## Questions and scope', '',
             'Which paper-backed releases complement the existing catalog? What are their counted units, property provenance and structural representations? Which access, reuse and source-lineage limits affect reuse? Isolated molecular or liquid-electrolyte collections are adjacent leads; they are not automatically promoted into the ranked crystal-materials catalog. Some retained optical and electrolyte resources contain mixed crystalline, amorphous or polymer populations, which their cards label explicitly.', '',
             '## OpenAlex search and verification', '',
             f'The search ran **{manifest["keyword_queries"]} keyword queries and one DDSE reference/citation traversal**, yielding **{manifest["returned_occurrences"]:,} returned occurrences and {manifest["distinct_works"]:,} distinct query-retrieved works**. Exact DOI metadata checks supplement that corpus. Queries had no year restriction; keyword runs requested up to 50 results, and DDSE traversal used a 100-result per-direction cap. No final result-list limit was applied. These caps, indexing differences and keyword selection limit recall. A retrieved work is not necessarily a dataset paper, and most retrieved works remain unreviewed leads.', '',
             'OpenAlex was searched automatically with the paper-search script. Primary publisher pages, author repositories and data deposits verified promoted releases. Crossref and Semantic Scholar were not additional systematic search corpora. CNKI and Wanfang were not searched: 英文库没检索到 ≠ 没人研究过. Some supplementary OpenAlex DOI requests returned HTTP 429; those failures are preserved, with independent query and primary-source evidence retained rather than inferred IDs.', '',
             '| Search run | Returned works | Recorded response |', '|---|---:|---|']
    for q in manifest['queries']:
        # Raw bodies are local caches; the tracked manifest preserves hashes/outcomes.
        lines += [f'| {cell(q["query"])} ({q["mode"]}) | {q["returned"]} | `{q["file"]}`; SHA-256 in receipt |']
    lines += ['', 'Raw publisher bodies, dataset payloads and caches remain local and ignored by Git. The normalized work ledger, source hashes, query outcomes and perspective decisions remain available. Counts are documentation-reported unless a card explicitly identifies an independent small-file recount.', '',
              '## DDSE is the earlier name of the DigBat lineage', '',
              'The requested paper is now explicitly linked in '+ref('digbat')+'. The original DDSE, DDSE 2.0 and DigBat are stages of one growing platform. The current catalog rank retains the June 2026 experimental-material count; earlier snapshots and measurement counts are additional denominators, not separate additive corpora.', '',
              '| Snapshot | Experimental materials | Experimental observations | Separate computational module | Evidence |', '|---|---:|---:|---|---|',
              '| Original DDSE, online 2023 / 2024 issue | 678 | Not substituted for material count | Not asserted from this source | [Original paper](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nanoms.2023.08.002) |',
              '| DDSE 2.0, 23 November 2024 | 2,349 | 18,309 performance records | 601 materials / 802 performance records | [Technical report](https://www.techscience.com/cmc/v81n3/59074/html) |',
              '| DigBat, June 2026 | 3,816 | 27,645 conductivity entries | 852 materials | [Provider announcement](https://www.tohoku.ac.jp/en/press/digbat_an_ai_ready_digital_platform_for_solid_state_battery_research.html) |', '',
              'The computational module supports structural visualization and VASP-format downloads, whereas experimental conductivity records carry temperature and sample context. Full experimental structure coverage and a bulk data redistribution license were not established for the platform.', '',
              '## Verified additions, grouped by catalog category', '',
              'Sizes descend within each existing category. Null sizes remain unranked. Each linked card provides count evidence, source release, access, rights, label conditions and overlap notes.', '',
              '| Dataset / release | Reported volume | Counted unit | Structure availability | Property provenance |', '|---|---:|---|---|---|']
    for d in sorted(chosen, key=lambda d:(d['category'],d['count'] is None,-(d['count'] or 0),d['name'])):
        lines += [f'| {ref(d["id"])} | {cell(d["count_display"])} | {cell(d["count_unit"])} | {d["structure_level"]} | {d["provenance"]} |']
    lines += ['', '## What changes across property families', '',
              '**Electrochemical transport.** '+ref('obelix')+' links 321 CIFs to a larger 599-material experimental cohort; '+ref('liverpool-ionics')+' counts 820 conductivity-at-temperature measurements rather than 820 unique compositions. DDSE/DigBat spans several ion and material classes, while these releases support narrower lithium-conductor studies. Measurement temperature, sample processing and label provenance must remain available when joining them.', '',
              'The '+ref('migration-barriers-literature-2025')+' archive counts pathways, whereas '+ref('polyanion-sodium-cathode-2025')+' counts atomistic configurations. Their 621 pathways and 298,144 frames do not represent the same sampling unit. The 619-record live migration repository and 621-record archived release are explicitly distinguished. The larger sodium cohort has charge labels for only a subset of its frames.', '',
              '**Ferroic and optical response.** '+ref('smidt-ferroelectric-2020')+' contains completed polar/nonpolar structure workflows; '+ref('ricci-polar-ferroelectrics-2024')+' reports a polarization-calculated cohort and smaller screening subsets. These are computed candidates, not experimentally demonstrated switching events. '+ref('trinquet-shg-2024')+' provides static nonlinear-response tensors, whereas '+ref('fang-wannier-optical-transport-2025')+' includes frequency/temperature-dependent electronic responses with model assumptions stated in its card.', '',
              'Large literature tables such as '+ref('cde-bandgaps-2022')+' and '+ref('cde-refractive-dielectric-2022')+' count records, not unique structure determinations. '+ref('ipop-v3')+' preserves host/dopant and luminescence observations; '+ref('ekhi-radiative-2026')+' counts experimental curves. These collections need material-state and measurement-condition filtering before comparison with crystal-specific computed labels.', '',
              '**Thermal and magnetic properties.** '+ref('tematdb272')+' preserves sample curve sets, while '+ref('estm-simd')+' counts composition-temperature observations. '+ref('wenzhou-te')+' is a computed database, and '+ref('nemad-thermoelectric')+' mixes experimental and theoretical source records. Electronic-only thermal conductivity or fixed-relaxation-time transport must not be interpreted as total measured thermal conductivity.', '',
              ref('nemad-magnetic')+' and '+ref('mce-llm-2024')+' address different magnetic observables and extraction pipelines. Their records can overlap older literature collections. The magnetocaloric release documents a paper-versus-current-file count discrepancy; extracted rows, corrected subsets and unique materials remain separate denominators.', '',
              '**Mechanical, storage and reactivity measurements.** '+ref('fatiguedata-cma2022')+' counts test-condition datasets, whereas '+ref('cu-alloys-mechanical-2023')+' counts processing/property/reference records. '+ref('polyverse-load-hardness')+' requires load-aware interpretation and carries custom reuse terms. Composition alone does not encode microstructure, specimen preparation or loading conditions.', '',
              ref('ml-hydpark')+' provides hydride storage and thermodynamic rows; '+ref('metal-combustion-properties')+' records alloy combustion measurements. Both are composition-level collections with experimental conditions and some derived quantities; neither supplies a new collection of atom-resolved crystal structures.', '',
              '## Coverage limits and unresolved checks', '',
              'Three newly included releases retain unknown sizes: TopoHSE-DB classifications, the PiezoML wurtzite archive and the Materials Cloud fast-lithium-conductor trajectory release. Their existence and data routes were verified without turning screened-candidate totals or archive byte sizes into labeled-record counts. Other deferred leads, including pure liquid-electrolyte datasets and releases with unresolved bulk access, remain in the perspective ledgers.', '',
              'A public page is distinct from a successfully downloaded payload, and article licensing is distinct from an external dataset license. Unknown rights remain explicit. HH130 download availability was not established after an HTTP 502 response. The NEMAD processed archive and full website have separately assessed rights. Source snapshots remain essential because repositories and papers can have different counts.', '',
              '## Evidence and candidate decisions', '',
              '- [Electrochemical search and primary-source notes](../research/openalex_property_20261101/electrochem/notes.md)',
              '- [Ferroic/optical search and primary-source notes](../research/openalex_property_20261101/ferroic/notes.md)',
              '- [Thermal/magnetic/mechanical search and primary-source notes](../research/openalex_property_20261101/transport/notes.md)',
              '- [Electrochemical candidate ledger](../research/openalex_property_20261101/electrochem/leads.json)',
              '- [Ferroic candidate ledger](../research/openalex_property_20261101/ferroic/leads.json)',
              '- [Thermal/mechanical candidate ledger](../research/openalex_property_20261101/transport/leads.json)',
              '- [Selected evidence and query entrypoints in source search](https://usccolumbia.github.io/matverse/?view=sources&collection=openalex_properties_20261101)', '',
              'The search identifies concrete complementary releases, but not a complete registry of every specialized property. Material/measurement distinction, method provenance and versioned rights determine which records can be joined; headline volume alone does not establish suitability for a scientific task.', '', '[Back to MatVerse](../README.md)', '']
    return '\n'.join(lines)
